### 🏗️ Auto-Sync Architecture

#### Layer 1 — Client-Side (Instant, No Server)
```typescript
// All time-based data calculated on the fly from fixed start dates
const AHMED_START_DATE = new Date('2022-01-01') // from CV — adjust to real date
const yearsOfExperience = calculateYears(AHMED_START_DATE) // auto-updates every year
```

#### Layer 2 — TanStack Query (Runtime Fetching with Smart Cache)
```typescript
// Repos auto-refresh every 30 minutes in background
const { data: repos } = useQuery({
  queryKey: ['github-repos'],
  queryFn: () => fetchGitHubRepos('ahmed-el-bialy'),
  staleTime: 30 * 60 * 1000,      // 30 minutes
  gcTime: 60 * 60 * 1000,         // 1 hour garbage collect
  refetchOnWindowFocus: true,      // refresh when user comes back to tab
  refetchInterval: 30 * 60 * 1000 // background refresh every 30 min
})
```

#### Layer 3 — Vercel Cron Jobs (Server-Side Scheduled Sync)
Create `/api/cron/sync-github.ts` — runs on Vercel's infrastructure:
```typescript
// vercel.json
{
  "crons": [
    {
      "path": "/api/cron/sync-github",
      "schedule": "0 */1 * * *"  // every hour
    },
    {
      "path": "/api/cron/sync-playstore",
      "schedule": "0 6 * * *"   // daily at 6am
    }
  ]
}
```
The cron fetches fresh data and writes to **Vercel KV** (key-value store) or **Edge Config**.
The client reads from KV — fast, cached, always fresh.

#### Layer 4 — Vercel KV Storage (Persistent Cache)
```typescript
// API route reads from GitHub, writes to KV
import { kv } from '@vercel/kv'

export async function GET() {
  const cached = await kv.get('github:repos')
  if (cached) return Response.json(cached)
  
  const fresh = await fetchFromGitHub()
  await kv.set('github:repos', fresh, { ex: 3600 }) // 1hr TTL
  return Response.json(fresh)
}
```

